 of Government securities, with the view to conducting the defense financing program with the greatest facility. The replies to Secretary Morgenthau's letter have been tabulated and the following tables have been made up to present some of the more important data. It should be noted that the reported data do not cover all of the commercial and savings banks and insurance companies in the country. They do cover, however, institutions that account for about 95 percent of the amount of United States Government and Government-guaranteed securities held by all banks and insurance companies.\n\nTable I.- Summary of Ownership by Type of Security, by Call Classes, and by Tax-Exemption Provision\n\n(Par value - in millions of dollars)\n\n| Classification > Classification > Unnamed: 0_level_2 | Total amount out-standing > Total amount out-standing > Unnamed: 1_level_2 | Held by institutions covered in Treasury survey > Total > Unnamed: 2_level_2 | Held by institutions covered in Treasury survey > 6,125 banks > Total | Held by institutions covered in Treasury survey > 6,125 banks > 5,638 commercial banks | Held by institutions covered in Treasury survey > 775 insurance companies > 487 mutual savings banks | Held by institutions covered in Treasury survey > 775 insurance companies > Total | Held by institutions covered in Treasury survey > 775 insurance companies > 200 life insurance companies | Held by all other investors > Held by all other investors > 575 fire, casualty, and marine insurance companies | Unnamed: 9_level_0 > Unnamed: 9_level_1 > Unnamed: 9_level_2 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A. By type of security | nan | nan | nan | nan | nan | nan | nan | nan | nan |\n| Treasury bills | 1604.0 | 645.0 | 611.0 | 566.0 | 45 | 34 | 1 | 32 | 959.0 |\n| Treasury notes | 5722.0 | 3360.0 | 3088.0 | 2875.0 | 213 | 272 | 179 | 93 | 2362.0 |\n| Treasury bonds | 29532.0 | 19107.0 | 13276.0 | 10478.0 | 2798 | 5831 | 4717 | 1114 | 10425.0 |\n| Pos